\fs32 \cf0 To show a homeowner's property using 
\f1\b USGS LiDAR Explorer
\f0\b0  data in Rails 8, you must extract a specific parcel bounding box, fetch the public LiDAR data, clip it, convert it, and render it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs40 \cf0 1. Extract the Property Spatial Boundary\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs32 \cf0 You need the geographic coordinates (bounding box) of the homeowner's property to isolate the point cloud.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Get the coordinates
\f0\b0 : Use a service like the USGS TNM Bureau of Land Management or a parcel data API to get the property's 
\f1\b Bounding Box (BBOX)
\f0\b0  in 
\f2\fs28 [MinX, MinY, MaxX, MaxY]
\f0\fs32  format.\
\ls6\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Coordinate reference
\f0\b0 : Note down the Spatial Reference System Identifier (SRID), usually 
\f1\b EPSG:4326
\f0\b0  (WGS 84 latitude/longitude) or a local 
\f1\b UTM zone
\f0\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs40 \cf0 2. Fetch and Clip the USGS LiDAR Data\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs32 \cf0 Instead of downloading massive, multi-gigabyte 
\f2\fs28 .laz
\f0\fs32  files manually, use 
\f1\b PDAL (Point Data Abstraction Library)
\f0\b0  to programmatically stream, clip, and save only the homeowner's property.\
Create a file named 
\f2\fs28 pipeline.json
\f0\fs32  in your Rails root:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs40 \cf0 json\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs28 \cf0 \{\
  "pipeline": [\
    \{\
      "type": "readers.ept",\
      "filename": "https://amazonaws.com",\
      "bounds": "([-8552300, -8552000], [4655300, 4655600])"\
    \},\
    \{\
      "type": "writers.las",\
      "filename": "public/pointclouds/property.laz"\
    \}\
  ]\
]\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 Use code with caution.\
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

